# Applies to everything under data/.
#
# Generated and reference data must round-trip through git byte-for-byte: the pipeline records
# SHA-256 checksums and promises byte-identical output across runs (brief rule 8). This repo
# checks out with core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite LF to CRLF in a fresh clone and change
# every checksum. "-text" tells git never to convert these files.
*.csv       -text
*.geojson   -text
*.json      -text
*.parquet   binary

# cmd.exe can fail to find goto/call labels in a batch file with LF line endings, so batch
# files are always checked out with CRLF whatever the local git settings are.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
